THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

The Work integrates with third-party software referenced by git
submodules under `agents/`, and at runtime calls third-party tools
installed by `docker/claude-config/scaffold-project.sh` and listed in
`agents/system-packages.txt`. Each third-party component remains
governed by its own upstream license; no claim of ownership over
third-party content is made by this license.

In particular:

  - `agents/buttercut/` is licensed by its authors under PolyForm
    Noncommercial 1.0.0 with a Commercial Output exception. The Work
    uses buttercut to produce video outputs ("Commercial Output") only
    in compliance with that exception. The Work does not bundle,
    redistribute, host, or sell buttercut itself as a commercial
    product, and the copyright holder asserts no rights over the
    buttercut tool.

  - All other Apache-2.0, MIT, BSD, ISC, MPL, and similarly licensed
    submodules are used in compliance with their notice and attribution
    requirements. Their LICENSE files are preserved within their
    respective submodule directories.

  - Submodules carrying copyleft licenses (GPL / AGPL / MPL family) are
    invoked at runtime as separate processes or as user-installed
    tools, not statically linked or redistributed as part of the Work.
    Their license boundaries are respected accordingly.

  - Where a submodule declares no explicit license, the Work treats it
    as "all rights reserved" by its authors and uses it only under
    fair-use research and personal-evaluation purposes pending
    clarification from the upstream authors.

